{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1529372-the-tribe-nemesis","id":1529372,"title":"The tribe nemesis","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-01-24T18:30:26-08:00","id":1529372,"title":"The tribe nemesis","content":"This is a backstory idea I had for a sort of final villain or almost that and I apologize for the names.<br /> <br /> &quot;Richard was once one of the proud Silver Fangs, but more out of consideration than anything. Edgar, Richard's father, had two Garou sons, one of them was the Ahroun Damian who was the son of his lawful partner and the second was Richard himself, the child of a passing romance, a moment of weakness that Edgar had in his youth so to speak, an accident, regardless of what you prefer to call it, he was an unplanned son and a stain on Edgar's reputation.<br /> <br /> Not much is known about Richard's childhood, but it is known that he grew up in a humble environment also didn't have a proper education and was barely literate. He was found by a pack of silver fangs when they heard rumors of what appeared to be a lost cub, it seems Richard had a premature first change. When brought to Edgar's camp (I just didn't think of a name) he soon found out about the boy's origin, however this was kept secret from most of the other members, Edgar considered sending him to another caern, preferably with another tribe, but chose to leave him nearby to watch over him, fearing that if he stayed out of sight he could cause trouble later, also an extra Garou could be useful.<br /> <br /> The years passed and Richard grew and became stronger, as did his half-brother Damian, both were promising soldiers and would probably both gain an important position in the future, the relationship between the two was close, Richard would be capable of dying for his companion, on the other hand, Edgar, the relationship between the two remained distant and was merely professional. Everything would change one night, Damian came to his father asking for advice, he had approached a girl, a Garou, things happened and now she was expecting a child, HIS CHILD, unfortunately for Edgar, she wasn't just any Garou, she came From an important bloodline, so he couldn't even try to get rid of her without repercussions, that's when his plan took shape: Blame Richard.<br /> <br /> Within days Richard was cornered, arrested, then tried for forced relations with another Garou, his peers, packmates, even his brother, no one spoke for him, not even an attempt to argue for him. Discredited, Richard manages to escape before being executed and for a while he lived in hiding, fleeing and killing Garous who were previously his brothers in arms. It didn't take long for the BSD to find him and offer him what he wanted most, power and revenge.<br /> <br /> Years later Richard would have returned to his old Caern with a contingent of BSDs and Wyrm creatures, Edgar managed to escape with his life, but Damian was captured by his half-brother and forced to dance the spiral and as if that weren't enough he was still taken to madness, turning him into nothing more than a mindless beast that attacks when commanded.&quot;<br /> <br /> So does this work as a backstory? Did I do something inconsistent? Did I forget to explain something? Too clich\u00e9? Sugestions?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}